  booktitle={Embodied Computing: Wearables, Implantables, Embeddables, Ingestibles}, 
  title={4 Cyborg Experiments and Hybrid Beings}, 
  year={2020},
  volume={},
  number={},
  pages={71-95},
  abstract={A cyborg is an entity made up of a biological and technological integration. Today the most common example of this is the merging together of a human with embedded technology of some kind into a new overall being. This, of course, raises issues as to the corresponding percentages of human and machine that make up the novel creature. Importantly, in a cyborg, a human and technology become an integrated system with capabilities different to and beyond the norm for a human.},
